Falsifies `jh7110_entropy::verification::a_128_bit_answer_is_never_served`.

The defect: `generation_outcome` never looks at `STAT.R256`, so a core left in 128-bit mode
answers `Ready` with all eight `RAND` words, four of which the generation never wrote. This is the
decode as it stood before `WrongOutputWidth` existed, and the bytes still look random, so nothing
downstream can notice.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(!matches!(outcome, GenerationOutcome::Ready(_)))`: a
seeded, idle core with `R256` clear and `RAND_RDY` set returns `Ready`.

